meta {
  name: Policy History
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/policies/{{soldPolicyId}}/history
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("always returns a chain, even for a policy never replaced", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.entries).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.entries.length).to.be.at.least(1);
    expect(body).to.have.property("totalChargeback");
  });

  test("marks the policy that was asked about", function () {
    const requested = res
      .getBody()
      .entries.filter(function (entry) {
        return entry.isRequested;
      });
    // Exactly one, whichever link in the chain was opened.
    expect(requested).to.have.lengthOf(1);
    expect(requested[0].policyId).to.equal(bru.getVar("soldPolicyId"));
  });

  test("is ordered oldest first and linked end to end", function () {
    const entries = res.getBody().entries;
    // Only the last entry is still in force; every earlier one names how it
    // ended.
    entries.forEach(function (entry, index) {
      if (index < entries.length - 1) {
        expect(entry.reason).to.be.oneOf(["cancel_rewrite", "company_transfer"]);
      } else {
        expect(entry.reason).to.equal(null);
      }
    });
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /policies/:id/history — the policy's full replacement chain

  Module `deal_audits` **or** `crm_service`, permission `deal_audits:read` or
  `crm_service:read` (the controller's OR gate — a CSR looking at a transferred
  policy has the same question as a producer looking at a rewritten one). Data
  scope is enforced by `loadOwnedPolicy`; out of scope 404s.

  Returns every policy in the chain the given policy belongs to — the ones that
  led to it **and** the ones that came after — oldest first. Served from any link
  in the chain and always returns the whole thing, because someone opening the
  original policy from two rewrites ago is asking the same question as someone
  opening the current one. The entry they asked about is flagged `isRequested`
  rather than being made the start.

  A policy that has never been replaced returns a **single-entry chain**, not a
  404 or an empty array, so a caller can render it without a "has history?"
  branch.

  ## Response `200`

  ```json
  {
    "entries": [
      {
        "policyId": "...",
        "policyNumber": "123456789",
        "policyType": "Auto",
        "carrier": "Allstate",
        "premium": 940,
        "status": "Cancel Rewrite",
        "active": false,
        "effectiveDate": "2026-01-05T00:00:00.000Z",
        "reason": "cancel_rewrite",
        "chargebackAmount": 940,
        "withinClawbackWindow": true,
        "dealId": "...",
        "isRequested": true
      },
      { "...": "the replacement, reason null, active true" }
    ],
    "totalChargeback": 940
  }
  ```

  `reason` is how that policy was **left**, and is `null` on the last entry —
  the one still in force. `chargebackAmount` / `withinClawbackWindow` are `null`
  where no chargeback was raised, which is every Company Transfer (a transfer
  moves a client within their own book; nothing is clawed back).

  The chain is walked, not aggregated, and is capped at 50 links with a cycle
  guard — the link fields are written as a pair inside one transaction and cannot
  legitimately loop, but a bad migration or hand-edit should truncate the history
  rather than hang the request.

  ## Errors

  | Code | When |
  |---|---|
  | `403` | Caller holds neither `deal_audits:read` nor `crm_service:read`, or both modules are disabled. |
  | `404` | No such policy, or it is outside the caller's data scope. |
}
